<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ r.client.title or (r.project ~ " model upgrade assessment") }}</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #fbfaf7; --surface: #ffffff; --text: #1d1d1b; --muted: #5f5d57; --line: #e4e1d8;
    --ship: #1f7a4d; --ship-bg: #e7f4ec; --caveat: #8a5a00; --caveat-bg: #fbf1dc;
    --dont: #a3261f; --dont-bg: #fbe7e5; --accent: #2d4a8a;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --bg: #151514; --surface: #1d1d1b; --text: #ecebe6; --muted: #a8a59c; --line: #34332f;
      --ship: #6fcf97; --ship-bg: #17301f; --caveat: #f2c14e; --caveat-bg: #33280f;
      --dont: #f28b82; --dont-bg: #3a1b18; --accent: #9db6f2;
    }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text);
         font: 16px/1.55 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif; }
  main { max-width: 920px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 16px 64px; }
  header p { color: var(--muted); margin: 4px 0 0; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.75rem; line-height: 1.25; margin: 0; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 40px 0 12px; }
  .verdict { margin-top: 28px; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px 24px; border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .verdict.ship { background: var(--ship-bg); border-color: var(--ship); }
  .verdict.ship_with_caveats { background: var(--caveat-bg); border-color: var(--caveat); }
  .verdict.dont_ship { background: var(--dont-bg); border-color: var(--dont); }
  .verdict .label { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 6px; }
  .ship .label { color: var(--ship); } .ship_with_caveats .label { color: var(--caveat); } .dont_ship .label { color: var(--dont); }
  .verdict ul { margin: 12px 0 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  .compare { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; }
  .card { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; }
  .card .k { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .card .v { font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 600; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  th, td { padding: 10px 12px; text-align: left; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
  tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  th { font-size: 0.8rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }
  td.n { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
  .desc { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .pill { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }
  .s-improved, .s-pass { background: var(--ship-bg); color: var(--ship); }
  .s-within_noise { background: var(--line); color: var(--text); }
  .s-regressed, .s-missing { background: var(--caveat-bg); color: var(--caveat); }
  .s-fail { background: var(--dont-bg); color: var(--dont); }
  .example { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .example .q { font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .answers { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; }
  .answer { border-left: 3px solid var(--line); padding-left: 12px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; font-size: 0.93rem; }
  .answer .who { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; display: block; margin-bottom: 4px; white-space: normal; }
  .answer.proposed { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  dl.explain dt { font-weight: 600; margin-top: 12px; }
  dl.explain dd { margin: 2px 0 0; color: var(--muted); }
  footer { margin-top: 48px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 16px; }
  @media print { body { background: #fff; } .verdict, .card, .table-wrap, .example { break-inside: avoid; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<header>
  <h1>{{ r.client.title or (r.project ~ ": model upgrade assessment") }}</h1>
  <p>Prepared {{ r.generated_at[:10] }}</p>
</header>

{% set primary = (c.metrics | selectattr("role", "equalto", "primary") | list)[0] %}
<section class="verdict {{ c.verdict }}">
  <p class="label">{{ r.verdict_label }}</p>
  {% if c.verdict == "ship" %}
  <p>The proposed configuration performs at least as well as the current one on every measure we track, within the tolerances agreed for this project.</p>
  {% elif c.verdict == "ship_with_caveats" %}
  <p>The proposed configuration is not meaningfully worse on the main quality measure, but some points need a decision before switching:</p>
  <ul>{% for reason in c.client_reasons %}<li>{{ reason }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
  {% else %}
  <p>The proposed configuration is measurably worse on a measure that matters, so we recommend staying on the current configuration for now:</p>
  <ul>{% for reason in c.client_reasons %}<li>{{ reason }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<h2>What we compared</h2>
<div class="compare">
  <div class="card"><div class="k">Current model</div><div class="v">{{ r.arms.baseline.model }}</div></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="k">Proposed model</div><div class="v">{{ c.model }}</div></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="k">Test set</div><div class="v">{{ r.dataset.examples }} questions × {{ r.repeats }} runs each</div></div>
</div>

<h2>Quality</h2>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Measure</th><th class="n">Current</th><th class="n">Proposed</th><th class="n">Change</th><th>Assessment</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for m in c.metrics %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ m.name|metric_name }}{% if m.role == "primary" %} <span class="desc">(main measure)</span>{% endif %}
        {% if r.metric_descriptions.get(m.name) %}<div class="desc">{{ r.metric_descriptions[m.name] }}</div>{% endif %}</td>
      {% if m.kind == "binary" %}
      <td class="n">{{ m.baseline|rate }}</td><td class="n">{{ m.candidate|rate }}</td>
      <td class="n">{{ (m.delta * 100 if m.delta is not none else none)|pts }}</td>
      {% else %}
      <td class="n">{{ m.baseline|num(2) }}</td><td class="n">{{ m.candidate|num(2) }}</td><td class="n">{{ m.delta|signed(3) }}</td>
      {% endif %}
      <td><span class="pill s-{{ m.status }}">{{ m.status|client_status(m.role) }}</span></td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h2>Cost and speed</h2>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table>
  <thead><tr><th></th><th class="n">Current</th><th class="n">Proposed</th><th class="n">Change</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Cost per question</td><td class="n">{{ c.cost.baseline.per_query_usd|usd }}</td><td class="n">{{ c.cost.candidate.per_query_usd|usd }}</td><td class="n">{{ c.cost.change_pct|change_pct }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Monthly cost at {{ "{:,}".format(c.cost.monthly_queries) }} questions</td><td class="n">{{ c.cost.baseline.monthly_usd|usd }}</td><td class="n">{{ c.cost.candidate.monthly_usd|usd }}</td><td class="n">{{ c.cost.monthly_delta_usd|usd_delta }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Typical response time</td><td class="n">{{ c.latency.baseline.p50_s|secs }}</td><td class="n">{{ c.latency.candidate.p50_s|secs }}</td><td class="n">{{ c.latency.p50_change_pct|change_pct }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Slow responses (95th percentile)</td><td class="n">{{ c.latency.baseline.p95_s|secs }}</td><td class="n">{{ c.latency.candidate.p95_s|secs }}</td><td class="n">{{ c.latency.p95_change_pct|change_pct }}</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

{% if examples %}
<h2>Example answers</h2>
{% for ex in examples %}
<div class="example">
  <div class="q">{{ ex.question|truncate_text(600) }}</div>
  <div class="answers">
    <div class="answer"><span class="who">Current</span>{{ ex.baseline_answer|truncate_text }}</div>
    <div class="answer proposed"><span class="who">Proposed{% if ex.direction == "improved" %} · better on {{ ex.metric|metric_name|lower }}{% elif ex.direction == "regressed" %} · worse on {{ ex.metric|metric_name|lower }}{% endif %}</span>{{ ex.candidate_answer|truncate_text }}</div>
  </div>
</div>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

<h2>How to read this</h2>
<dl class="explain">
  <dt>Both configurations answered the same questions</dt>
  <dd>Every comparison is made question by question, so differences in question difficulty cancel out. Each question was answered {{ r.repeats }} times by each configuration and the results averaged.</dd>
  <dt>“No real change”</dt>
  <dd>We measured how much the current configuration's own scores move between identical runs. A difference smaller than that run-to-run variation is not a real change and is never counted as a regression.</dd>
  <dt>“No meaningful drop”</dt>
  <dd>The goal of an upgrade is usually to be no worse on quality while being cheaper or faster, not to be strictly better. For the main measure, a drop is meaningful when it could exceed {{ (r.decision.primary_margin|abs * 100)|round(1) }} points on a 0–100 scale.</dd>
  <dt>What this does not cover</dt>
  <dd>The results describe this test set and these measures. They are strong evidence, not a guarantee about every future question, which is why we keep monitoring after a switch.</dd>
</dl>

<footer>
  {{ r.dataset.examples }} test questions · {{ r.repeats }} runs per configuration · answers graded by {{ r.judge.model }} with fixed settings · generated {{ r.generated_at[:10] }}
</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
